      "math_academy_id": "q-86728",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{b\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 5+(-2)\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot (-3)}{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0+(-12)+6}{4+0+4+4}b \\\\  & =\\frac{-6}{12}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
